                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "264433ee-30a0-35fa-92b4-4c9d640a1654",
                        "entry_id": "4a420d24-36ec-3c62-b5ab-b01eeb05d171",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An executioner whose method of dispatching the condemned is decapitation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "77e8d11d-0fda-47c1-885a-75224237bed5",
                                "sense_id": "264433ee-30a0-35fa-92b4-4c9d640a1654",
                                "text": "And of those base-minded jesters or buffons, some have beene seene, that even at the point of death would never leave their jesting and scoffing. He whom the heads-man threw off from the Gallowes cried out, ‘Row the Gally,’ which was his ordinarie by-word."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e113ed7-147d-489f-8538-c58a2b616280",
                                "sense_id": "264433ee-30a0-35fa-92b4-4c9d640a1654",
                                "text": "And made him Headsman, for we said, / \"Who's next to be decapited / Cannot cut off another's head / Until he's cut his own off[…]\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9251e741-2bdb-31d2-842b-3e496fd83e07",
                        "entry_id": "4a420d24-36ec-3c62-b5ab-b01eeb05d171",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A labourer in a colliery who transports the coal from the workings to the horseway, and who is oftentimes assisted by a younger worker called a foal."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
